WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.940
In a purported breakdown of the first two-thirds
of The Rise of Skywalker's plot, Reddit user

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.690
JediPaxis has claimed that something major
goes on at the end of the movie's second act.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.030
Specifically, someone Star Wars fans said
goodbye to just a few years ago will supposedly

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.240
make an epic, unexpected return.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.830
A rumored crucial part of The Rise of Skywalker
could involve the inner turmoil of Adam Driver's

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.830
Kylo Ren.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.369
The former Ben Solo has spent his adult life
striving to emulate Darth Vader, by rising

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:29.890
through the ranks of the First Order and pledging
allegiance to the Empire.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.100
His path has been pretty dark throughout The
Force Awakens and The Last Jedi, but some

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.570
fans have theorized that the new Supreme Leader
could be redeemed in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.760
How might that happen?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.890
"I had a blast today.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:47.440
I really learned a lot, and people are gonna
love the new me."

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.219
According to some fans, none other than Kylo's
father, Han Solo, played by Harrison Ford,

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:56.460
will return in The Rise of Skywalker and offer
his son a chance at redemption.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.110
The moment allegedly happens after Kylo and
Rey engage in a tense lightsaber battle, during

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.839
which both Force-sensitive fighters can feel
that Leia is dying.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:08.900
This heightens their emotions, and pushes
Rey to grab Kylo's weapon and drive it through

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.900
his chest.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.560
She tells Kylo that she will never be like
him before summoning her newfound healing

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.740
ability to save Kylo from death.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.610
Afterwards, Rey steals Kylo's ship and Darth
Vader's wayfinder device to head to Endor,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.909
leaving Kylo broken and defeated.

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:27.009
It's here where Han Solo reportedly appears
to Kylo as a vision and tells him that it's

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:30.759
never too late to return to return to the
light and make the right choice.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:34.380
Kylo is said to be moved by the conversation
with his late father and decides to become

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.730
Ben Solo again, thus returning to the light
side.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.790
The idea of Kylo Ren stripping away his dark
persona, reclaiming his birth name of Ben

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:46.491
Solo, and turning to the light side is an
intriguing thought, but will it actually happen

00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:47.950
in The Rise of Skywalker?

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:52.150
Similarly, will Harrison Ford actually circle
back to the Star Wars franchise to play the

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.040
character whose son killed him in cold blood?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.891
Neither are out of the realm of possibility,
given that some pretty wild stuff has gone

00:01:58.891 --> 00:02:01.290
on in the Star Wars universe before.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:05.291
As fans have heard at least 100 times since
news of Episode IX first broke, the movie

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.220
will bring the Skywalker saga to a definitive
end.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.790
Could this final film showcase the last fight
between the First Order and the Resistance,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.420
as well as a redemption for Kylo Ren?

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.550
Star Wars has brought dead characters back
as force ghosts and visions before, so it's

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:23.020
not unreasonable to think that Han would resurface
as a vision to his son, offering him guidance

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.980
at the lowest point in his life.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.060
Still, Kylo did straight-up kill Han in The
Force Awakens, so there's something to be

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.680
said about whether Han is the person Kylo
needs strength from.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.381
Another thing worth considering when pondering
the possibility of Han Solo returning in The

00:02:36.381 --> 00:02:40.570
Rise of Skywalker is whether Harrison Ford
would want to be a part of the film.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:45.260
As Ford told Jimmy Kimmel, he'd been pushing
for Solo to die for almost 30 years, so that

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.880
may mean that he considers the death the ultimate
culmination of the character.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.800
"I argued for 30 years for this to happen.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.330
Finally, I wore them down."

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.280
Still, there's really no better way to bring
him back to the franchise than by helping

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.020
redeem his wayward son.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:07.090
There's also the chance that this alleged
plot breakdown holds no weight and what actually

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.160
happens in The Rise of Skywalker isn't even
remotely close to what's rumored.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.440
Kylo could stay on the dark side, Han Solo
could stay offscreen, and a completely different

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.550
sequence of events could unravel.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.940
Fans will simply have to wait to learn the
truth when The Rise of Skywalker arrives in

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.810
theaters on December 20.

